          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theory/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            called
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            – for
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} topological modular forms
            – is in a precise sense the union of all
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology+theories"} elliptic cohomology theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+spectra"} elliptic spectra
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hopkins94"}> Hopkins 94
            ).
          %p
            More precisely,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+spectra"} elliptic spectra
            of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            theories, parameterized over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi ell
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goerss-Hopkins-Miller+theorem"} Goerss-Hopkins-Miller theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            this refines the
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            to an
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{M}_{ell}, \mathcal{O}^{top})
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Deligne-Mumford+stack"} spectral Deligne-Mumford stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+sections"} global sections
            of that structure sheaf (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"}> Lurie
            ).
          %p
            The construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            has motivation from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"}> string theory
            ) and from
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %strong
                  from
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                Associating to a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
                of the
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
                with that space as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                defines a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
                known as the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
                in ordinary
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                (the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientations
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theories"} multiplicative cohomology theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-hat+genus"} A-hat genus
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
                of the
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+particle"} spinning particle
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superparticle"} superparticle
                is a shadow of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Bott-Shapiro+orientation"} Atiyah-Bott-Shapiro
                = succeed "-orientation" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+structure"} Spin structure
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
                spectrum. Therefore an obvious question is which spectrum lifts this classical statement from point
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi tmf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
                solves this: there is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+structure"} String structure
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+orientation+of+tmf"} orientation of tmf
                such that on homotopy groups it reduces to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                (
                %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk10"}> Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10
                ).
              %p
                Mathematically this means for instance that
                = succeed "-cohomology" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi tmf
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+structure"} string
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                which is captured by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
                is realized more deeply as part of fundamental mathematics (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                is still under investigation, this might point the way:
              %blockquote
                %p
                  A properly developed theory of elliptic cohomology is likely to shed some light on what
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                  really means. (
                  %a{:href => "#Witten87"}> Witten 87, very last sentence
                  )
            %li
              %p
                %strong
                  from
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} (∞,1)-category of spectra
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+spectra"}> finite spectra
                ) has its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+spectrum+of+a+symmetric+monoidal+stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} prime spectrum
                parameterized by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+numbers"} prime numbers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+K-theory"} Morava K-theory
                spectra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(n)
                at these primes, for natural numbers
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                here is called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+level"} chromatic level
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
                and that at level 1 is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi tmf
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#MazelGee13"} Mazel-Gee 13
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "#Behrens13"} Behrens 13
                = succeed "))." do
                  %a{:href => "#Hopkins02"} Hopkins 02
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
                this means for instance that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi tmf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
                provides new tools for computing more
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} homotopy groups of spheres
                via an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams-Novikov+spectral+sequence"} Adams-Novikov spectral sequence
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p Write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi cub
