            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi ell
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
                for the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mover
                          %mi ell
                          %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{\overline{ell}}
                for its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+compactification"} Deligne-Mumford compactification
                obtained by adding the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+cubic+curve"} nodal cubic curve
          %p
            (Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi cub
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{cub}
            is obatined by furthermor adding also the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cuspidal+cubic+curve"} cuspidal cubic curve
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi ell
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mover
                        %mi ell
                        %mo ¯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi cusp
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi FG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}\to \mathcal{M}_{\overline{ell}}\to \mathcal{M}_{cusp} \to \mathcal{M}_{FG}
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goerss-Hopkins-Miller+theorem"} Goerss-Hopkins-Miller theorem
            equips these three moduli stacks with
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaves"} structure sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}
            (and by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"} Lurie (Survey)
            that makes them into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Deligne-Mumford+stacks"} spectral Deligne-Mumford stacks
            which are moduli spaces for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+elliptic+curves"} derived elliptic curves
            etc.)
          %p
            The
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi tmf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
              \-spectrum
            is defined to be the
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+sections"} global sections
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}
            (in the sense of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+site"} etale site
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TMF
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi ell
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TMF \coloneqq \Gamma(\mathcal{M}_{ell}, \mathcal{O}^{top})
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Tmf
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mover
                          %mi ell
                          %mo ¯
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tmf \coloneqq \Gamma(\mathcal{M}_{\overline{ell}}, \mathcal{O}^{top})
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi tmf
                      %mo ≔
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf \coloneqq
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+cover"} connective cover
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Tmf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tmf
                (also
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mover
                          %mi cub
                          %mo ¯
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq \Gamma(\mathcal{M}_{\overline{cub}}, \mathcal{O}^{top})
                (
                %a{:href => "#HillLawson13}"} Hill-Lawson 13, p. 2
                (?)).
          %h2#constructions Constructions
          %h3#DecomopositionViaArithmeticSquares Decomposition via Arithmetic fracture squares
          %p
            We survey here some aspects of the explicit construction in (
            %a{:href => "#Behrens13"}> Behrens 13
            ), a review is also in (
            %a{:href => "#MazelGee13"}> Mazel-Gee 13
            ),
          %p
            The basic strategy here is to use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+squares"} arithmetic squares
            in order to decompose the problem into smaller more manageable pieces.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi ell
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathcal{M}_{ell}}
            for the compactified
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ℳ
                                %mi ell
                            %mo ¯
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ι
                                %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ℳ
                                %mi ell
                            %mo ¯
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ι
                                  %mi ℚ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ℳ
                                %mi ell
                            %mo ¯
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\overline{\mathcal{M}_{ell}}
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\iota_{p}}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                  (\overline{\mathcal{M}_{ell}})_p
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{\iota_{\mathbb{Q}}}}\uparrow
                  \\\
                  (\overline{\mathcal{M}_{ell}})_{\mathbb{Q}}
                  }
          %p
            given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi ell
                    %mo ¯
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ℚ
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi ell
                    %mo ¯
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\overline{\mathcal{M}_{ell}})_{\mathbb{Q}}
                  \=
                  \\overline{\mathcal{M}_{ell}}
                  \\underset{Spec(\mathbb{Z})}{\times}
                  Spec(\mathbb{Q})
          %p
            (hence this is the moduli of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "elliptic+curve#OverTheRationalNumbers"} elliptic curves over the rational numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-completion"} p-completion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi ell
                    %mo ¯
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi ell
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Spf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\overline{\mathcal{M}_{ell}})_p
                  \=
                  (\overline{\mathcal{M}_{ell}})
                  \\underset{Spec(\mathbb{Z})}{\times}
                  Spf(\mathbb{Z}_p)
          %p
            for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_p
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+integers"} p-adic integers
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spf(-)
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+spectrum"} formal spectrum
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "elliptic+curve#OverpAdics"} elliptic curves over p-adic integers
          %p
            This induces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+square"} arithmetic square
            decomposition which realizes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi top
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mi p
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo *
                          %msubsup
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi p
                            %mi top
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi L
                                  %mi ℚ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mi ℚ
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo *
                          %msubsup
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mi top
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mi arith
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                                %mi p
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi ι
                                %mi p
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo *
                              %msubsup
                                %mi 𝒪
                                %mi p
                                %mi top
                              %mo )
                            %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathcal{O}^{top} &amp;\to&amp; \prod_p (\iota_p)_\ast \mathcal{O}^{top}_p
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{L_{\mathbb{Q}}}}
                  \\\
                  (\iota_{\mathbb{Q}})_\ast \mathcal{O}^{top}_{\mathbb{Q}}
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\alpha_{arith}}{\to}&amp;
                  \\left(
                  \\prod_p (\iota_p)_\ast \mathcal{O}^{top}_p
                  \\right)_{\mathbb{Q}}
                  }
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}_{\mathbb{Q}}
            can be obtained directly, and to obtain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi p
                    %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}_p
            one uses in turn another
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fracture+square"} fracture square
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%28n%29-localization"} K(n)-localization
            into
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(1)
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(2)
          %p (…)
          %h3#stacks_from_spectra Stacks from spectra
          %p
            There is a way to “construct” the tmf-spectrum as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} structured (∞,1)-topos
            whose underlying space is essentially the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
          %h4#the_context__derived_geometry_over_formal_duals_of_rings
            The context – derived geometry over formal duals of
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %p
            The discussion happens in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} small
            version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            of formal duals of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical coverage
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi Ring
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in E_\infty Ring
            we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
            for its image under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi Ring
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ↪
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_\infty Ring)^{op} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{H}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} terminal object
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              is the formal dual of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    * \simeq Spec(\mathbb{S})
                    \\,.
            %p
              Because the sphere spectrum is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn ∞
                      %mi Ring
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty Ring
          %h4#coverings_by_the_thom_spectrum Coverings by the Thom spectrum
          %p The crucial input for the entire construction is the following statement.
          %p
            The idea is that the formal dual of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology"} complex cobordism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U
            is in a suitable sense a covering
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Spec M U \to  Spec \mathbb{S}
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Adams%20spectral%20sequence#DefinitionInHigherAlgebra"} Adams spectral sequence – As derived descent
          %p
            This means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec M U
            plays the role of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            of the point. This allows to do some computations with ring spectra
            %em
              locally on the cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec M U
            \. Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U^*
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard+ring"} Lazard ring
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+law"} formal group law
          %p
            To see this, first notice that the problem of realizing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = tmf
            or any other ring spectrum as the ring of global sections on something has a
            %em tautological solution
            \: almost by definition (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+scheme"} generalized scheme
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}Spec(R)
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
            and its global sections is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  tmf \simeq \mathcal{O}(Spec(tmf))
                  \\,.
          %p
            In order to get a less tautological and more insightful characterization, the strategy is now to pass on the right to the
            = succeed "-cover" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec M U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi tmf
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi tmf
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi M
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Spec(tmf) \times Spec(M U) &amp;\to&amp; Spec(tmf)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  Spec(M U) &amp;\to&amp; * \simeq Spec(\mathbb{S})
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            The resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object in an (∞,1)-category
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi MU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi MU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi MU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \stackrel{\to}{\stackrel{\to}{\to}} Spec(tmf) \times Spec(MU) \times Spec(MU) \stackrel{\to}{\to} Spec(tmf) \times Spec(MU)
          %p which by formal duality is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi MU
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi MU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi MU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \stackrel{\to}{\stackrel{\to}{\to}} Spec (tmf \wedge MU \wedge MU) \stackrel{\to}{\to} Spec ( tmf \wedge MU)
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∧
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge
            of ring spectra over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            operation on function algebras formally dual to forming products of spaces.
          %p
            As a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object
            this is still equivalent to just
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi tmf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(tmf)
          %h4#decategorification_the_ordinary_moduli_stack_of_elliptic_curves Decategorification: the ordinary moduli stack of elliptic curves
          %p
            To simplify this we take a drastic step and apply a lot of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            to all the
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi tmf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_*(tmf)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_*(M U)
            etc. The result is an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \stackrel{\to}{\stackrel{\to}{\to}} Spec (\pi_*(tmf \wedge M U \wedge  M U)) \stackrel{\to}{\to} Spec ( \pi_*(tmf \wedge M U))
                  \\,,
          %p
            which remembers the fact that its structure rings are graded by being equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the multiplicative group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔾
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G} = \mathbb{A}^\times
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+object"} line object
          %p
            This general Ansatz is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Hopkins"}> Hopkins
            ).
          %p
            This simplicial scheme, which is degreewise the formal dual of a graded ring of
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized homology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi ell
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#HenriquesModuli"} Henriques
          %p
            In fact if in this construction one replaced
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec tmf
            by the point, one obtains the simplicial scheme
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \stackrel{\to}{\stackrel{\to}{\to}} Spec (\pi_*(M U \wedge M U)) \stackrel{\to}{\to} Spec ( \pi_*(M U))
          %p
            which one finds is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+formal+group+laws"} moduli stack of formal group laws
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi fg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{fg}
          %h4#explicit_computation_of_homotopy_groups_by_a_spectral_sequence Explicit computation of homotopy groups by a spectral sequence
          %p
            Now, a priori these underived stacks remember little about the original
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec tmf
            etc. They may not even carry any
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %p
            If they do carry an
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi q
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^p(\mathcal{M}_{ell}, \pi_q(\mathcal{O}))
                  \\Rightarrow
                  \\pi_{p+q} \mathcal{O}(\mathcal{M}_{ell})
                  \\,.
          %p
            But it turns out that even if the derived structure sheaf does not exist, this spectral sequence may still converge and may still compute the homotopy groups of the ring spectrum that one started with. This gives one way to compute the homotopy groups of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi tmf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
          %p
            For the case of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            one finds that the homotopy sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_q(\mathcal{O}(\mathcal{M}_{ell}))
            are simple: they vanish in odd degree and are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+power"} tensor power
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega^{\otimes k}
            of the canonical line bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            in even degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
            of that curve at its identity element. A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega^{\otimes k}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+form"} modular form
            of weight
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            boils down to computing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            of the moduli stack of elliptic curves with coefficients in these abelian groups of modular forms — and then examining the resulting spectral sequence.
          %p
            This can be done quite explicitly in terms of a long but fairly elementary computation in ordinary algebra. A detailed discussion of this computation is in (
            %a{:href => "#Henriques"}> Henriques
            )
          %h3#WithLevelStructure With Level structure
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            has covers by that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves+with+level+structure"} elliptic curves with level structure
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}
            and hence induce spectra of “topological forms with level structure”,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf(\Gamma)
            (
            %a{:href => "#MahowaldRezk09"}> Mahowald-Rezk 09
            ). For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} modular equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %p
            For instance
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi tmf
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf_0(2)
            (for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence+subgroup"} congruence subgroup
            which preserves an NS-R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            on elliptic curves over the complex numbers) is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+spectrum"} elliptic spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ell
            of (
            %a{:href => "#spin+orientation+of+Ochanine+elliptic+cohomology#LandweberRavenelStong93"}> Landweber-Ravenel-Stong 93
            ), see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf0%282%29"} tmf0(2)
          %p
            Discussion of level structure also governs the relation of tmf to K-theory, see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#MapToTateKTheory"} Maps to K-theory and Tate K-theory
          %h2#properties Properties
