          %h2#references References
          %p
            The idea of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            the ring of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} topological modular forms
            providing a home for the refined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            of
          %ul
            %li#Witten87a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Elliptic Genera And Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104117076"} euclid.cmp/1104117076
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://people.maths.ox.ac.uk/beem/papers/elliptic_genus_witten.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and produced as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            theories over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            was originally announced, as joint work with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Mahowald"} Mark Mahowald
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haynes+Miller"} Haynes Miller
          %ul
            %li#Hopkins94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
              , section 9 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological modular forms, the Witten Genus, and the theorem of the cube
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Hopkins_TopModFormsAtICM.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-0348-9078-6_49"} doi:10.1007/978-3-0348-9078-6_49
          %p
            (There the spectrum was still called “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi eo
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} eo_2
            ” instead of “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            ”.) The details of the definition then appeared in
          %ul
            %li#Hopkins02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
              , section 4 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic topology and modular forms
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212397"} arXiv:math/0212397
          %p
            A central tool that goes into the construction is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goerss-Hopkins-Miller+theorem"} Goerss-Hopkins-Miller theorem
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li#DFHH14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Douglas"}> Christopher Douglas
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"} John Francis
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"} André Henriques
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hill"} Michael Hill
              (eds.),
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological Modular Forms
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-201"} ISBN:978-1-4704-1884-7
          %p Expositions include
          %ul
            %li#MazelGee13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Mazel-Gee"}> Aaron Mazel-Gee
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    You could’ve invented
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi tmf
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~aaron/writing/ustars-tmf-beamer.pdf"} pdf slides
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~aaron/writing/tmf-seminar-talk.pdf"} notes pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Douglas"}> Chris Douglas
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"} André Henriques
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological modular forms and conformal nets
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              (eds.),
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1103.4187"} arXiv:1103.4187
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/pspum/083"} doi:10.1090/pspum/083
          %p
            An actual detailed account of the construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            (via decomposition by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+squares"} arithmetic squares
          %ul
            %li#Behrens13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Behrens"}> Mark Behrens
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Notes on the construction of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi tmf
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~mbehrens/papers/buildTMF.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A complete account of the computation of the homotopy groups of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            (following previous unpublished computations) is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tilman+Bauer"}> Tilman Bauer
              ,
              %em
                Computation of the homotopy groups of the spectrum
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi tmf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/eo2ss.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A survey of how this works is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
                ,
                %em
                  The homotopy groups of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi TMF
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TMF
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.uchicago.edu/~amathew/tmfhomotopy.pdf"}> pdf
                )
              %p
                (This presents as an instructive much simpler but analogous case the construction of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
                in analogy to the construction of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi tmf
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a{:href => "#Mathew13"} Mathew 13, section 3
          %p and course notes that go through the construction of tmf and the computation of its homotopy groups are here:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em Talbot workshop on TMF
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/2007/tmfproc/"}> web
                )
              %ul
                %li#Hopkins
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
                    (talk notes by
                    = succeed ")," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hill"} Michael Hill
                    %em Stacks and complex oriented cohomology theories
                    (
                    %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/2007/tmfproc/Chapter08/MikesTalk1.pdf"}> pdf
                    )
                %li#Henriques
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"}> André Henriques
                    ,
                    %em The homotopy groups of tmf
                    (
                    %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/2007/tmfproc/Chapter16/TmfHomotopy.pdf"}> pdf
                    )
                %li#HenriquesModuli
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"}> André Henriques
                    ,
                    %em The moduli stack of elliptic curves
                    (
                    %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/2007/tmfproc/Chapter04/henriques.pdf"}> pdf
                    )
          %p The non-connective version of this is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johan+Konter"}> Johan Konter
              ,
              %em The homotopy groups of the spectrum Tmf
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1212.3656"}> arXiv:1212.3656
              )
          %p Supplementary material graphically displaying parts of these intricate computations is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"}> André Henriques
                ,
              %p
                the graded ring
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi tmf
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi pt
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf^\ast(pt)
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.staff.science.uu.nl/~henri105/PDF/TmfRing.pdf"}> pdf
                );
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
                used to compute it (
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/2007/tmfproc/henriques-tmfSS.pdf"}> pdf
                );
              %p
                whose
                = succeed "-page" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ext
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext_{A(2)}(\mathbb{F}_2, \mathbb{F}_2)
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(2)
                is displayed here:
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.staff.science.uu.nl/~henri105/PDF/A2.pdf"} pdf
              %p
                the spectral sequence that computes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Tmf
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi pt
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tmf^\ast(pt)
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/2007/tmfproc/EllipticSpectralSequence.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Mathew13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
              ,
              %em
                The homology of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi tmf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1305.6100"}> arXiv:1305.6100
              )
          %p
            The refinement of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            to a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi tmf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+orientation+of+tmf"} string orientation of tmf
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological modular forms, the Witten Genus, and the theorem of the cube
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathunion.org/ICM/ICM1994.1/Main/icm1994.1.0554.0565.ocr.pdf"} pdf
            %li#AndoHopkinsStrickland01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"} Neil Strickland
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elliptic spectra, the Witten genus and the theorem of the cube
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic topology and modular forms
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212397"} arXiv:math/0212397
            %li#AndoHopkinsRezk10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Charles Rezk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Multiplicative orientations of KO-theory and the spectrum of topological modular forms
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/~mando/papers/koandtmf.pdf"} pdf
          %p see also remark 1.4 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              %em Topological modular forms (after Hopkins, Miller and Lurie)
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/arxiv/pdf/0910/0910.5130v1.pdf"}> pdf
              ).
          %p
            and for more on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-orientation"} sigma-orientation
            see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The sigma orientation for analytic circle-equivariant elliptic cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0201092"} arXiv:math/0201092
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            is in
          %ul
            %li#ABG10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"} Andrew Blumberg
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twists of K-theory and TMF
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"} Jonathan Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Superstrings, Geometry, Topology, and
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bookstore-getitem/item=PSPUM-81"} vol 81
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3004"} arXiv:1002.3004
          %p
            Topological modular forms with
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+N-structure"} level N-structure
            –
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf(N)
            – is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#MahowaldRezk09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Mahowald"}> Mark Mahowald
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Charles Rezk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological modular forms of level 3
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/~rezk/tmf3-paper-final.pdf"} pdf
            %li#DavisMahowald10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Davis"}> Donald Davis
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Mahowald"} Mark Mahowald
                %em
                  Connective versions of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi TMF
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TMF(3)
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1005.3752"}> arXiv:1005.3752
                )
            %li#Stojanoska11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vesna+Stojanoska"}> Vesna Stojanoska
                , Duality for Topological Modular Forms (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1105.3968"}> arXiv:1105.3968
                )
            %li#LawsonNaumann12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tyler+Lawson"}> Tyler Lawson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niko+Naumann"} Niko Naumann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strictly commutative realizations of diagrams over the Steenrod algebra and topological modular forms at the prime 2
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.1696"} arXiv:1203.1696
            %li#HillLawson13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hill"}> Michael Hill
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tyler+Lawson"} Tyler Lawson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological modular forms with level structure
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1312.7394"} arXiv:1312.7394
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00222-015-0589-5"} doi:10.1007/s00222-015-0589-5
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (with
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+structure+on+an+elliptic+curve"} level structure
          %p
            The self-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anderson+duality"} Anderson duality
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Stojanoska11"}> Stojanoska 11
            ).
          %p
            On equivariant topological modular forms (on
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"}> David Gepner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lennart+Meier"} Lennart Meier
              = succeed "," do
                %em On equivariant topological modular forms
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.10254"} arXiv:2004.10254
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman+homomorphism"} Boardman homomorphism
            (generalized
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+homomorphism"} Hurewicz homomorphism
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman+homomorphism"} Boardman homomorphism
            (generalized
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+homomorphism"} Hurewicz homomorphism
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Behrens"}> Mark Behrens
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Mahowald"} Mark Mahowald
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+D.+Quigley"} J. D. Quigley
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The 2-primary Hurewicz image of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi tmf
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
              %strong 27
              (2023) 2763–2831 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.08956"}> arXiv:2011.08956
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/gt.2023.27.2763"} doi:10.2140/gt.2023.27.2763
          %p
            More on the role of lifting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            to tmf from the point of view of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuji+Tachikawa"}> Yuji Tachikawa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological modular forms and the absence of a heterotic global anomaly
                %strong 2022
                4 (2022) 04A107
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.12211"} arXiv:2103.12211
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/ptep/ptab060"} doi:10.1093/ptep/ptab060
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuji+Tachikawa"}> Yuji Tachikawa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mayuko+Yamashita"} Mayuko Yamashita
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological modular forms and the absence of all heterotic global anomalies
                %strong 402
                (2023) 1585-1620 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.13542"}> arXiv:2108.13542
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-023-04761-2"} doi:10.1007/s00220-023-04761-2
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuji+Tachikawa"}> Yuji Tachikawa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mayuko+Yamashita"} Mayuko Yamashita
                %em Anderson self-duality of topological modular forms, its differential-geometric manifestations, and vertex operator algebras
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.06196"}> arXiv:2305.06196
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+operations"} Adams operations
            for tmf:
          %ul
            %li
              Jack Morgan Davies,
              %em Constructing and calculating Adams operations on dualisable topological modular forms
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13407"}> arXiv:2104.13407
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
